We agree that we shall not during our relationship or after its termination (however caused), disclose 
or use in any manner whatsoever, any confidential knowledge, information, intellectual property or 
any financial trading information relating to either party or to any former or existing employee and/or 
client of either party. 
It is agreed that such information can only be disclosed by either party’s request or if ordered by a 
court of competent jurisdiction and only in a manner consistent with such order. 
On the subject of either party supplying information, copies of documents, etc, during the course of 
the two-party’s involvement, both parties hereby confirm as follows: 
1. That all information, whenever disclosed by either party to the other party, shall remain the 
property of the disclosing party. 
2. Neither party will use the information disclosed by the other for any purpose other than in 
connection with the two parties’ involvement. Each party shall keep all disclosed information 
secret and confidential. Neither party shall, without consent of the disclosing party, communicate 
or allow to be communicated any confidential information to anyone, except as otherwise 
authorised by the disclosing party. 
3. Both parties confirm their acceptance of the retention by each party of their existing rights. 
4. This agreement shall not apply to any information which was in either party’s possession prior to 
the time of disclosure; in the public domain prior to disclosure; becomes part of the public domain 
not due to any unauthorised act or omission on either party’s part; or, is supplied to the party by a 
third party as a matter of right. 
 
 
